ch side of the hexagon is the same as the side of the equilateral triangle, which is 7 inches. Therefore, the perimeter of the hexagon is \\( 6 \\times 7 = 42 \\) inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given perimeter of one equilateral triangle\nperimeter_triangle = 21\n\n# Number of sides in an equilateral triangle\nsides_triangle = 3\n\n# Side length of the equilateral triangle\nside_length = perimeter_triangle / sides_triangle\n\n# Number of sides in a regular hexagon\nsides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Perimeter of the regular hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length * sides_hexagon\nprint(perimeter_hexagon)\n```\n```output\n42.0\n```\nThe perimeter of the regular hexagon is \\(\\boxed{42}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to understand the relationship between the perimeter of one equilateral triangle and the perimeter of the hexagon.\n\n1. **Understand the Perimeter of the Equilateral Triangle:**\n   - Since the triangle is equilateral, all three sides are equal.\n   - If the perimeter of the equilateral triangle is 21 inches, then each side of the triangle is \\( \\frac{21}{3} = 7 \\) inches.\n\n2. **Understand the Hexagon:**\n   - A regular hexagon can be divided into six equilateral triangles.\n   - The side length of the hexagon is the same as the side length of each of these equilateral triangles.\n   - Since each side of the hexagon is 7 inches, the perimeter of the hexagon is \\( 6 \\times 7 = 42 \\) inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given perimeter of the equilateral triangle\nperimeter_triangle = 21\n\n# Calculate the side length of the equilateral triangle\nside_length_triangle = perimeter_triangle / 3\n\n# The side length of the hexagon is the same as the side length of the equilateral triangle\nside_length_hexagon = side_length_triangle\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = 6 * side_length_hexagon\nprint(perimeter_hexagon)\n```\n```output\n42.0\n```\nTh