b^2 + 20a^3b^3 + 15a^2b^4 + 6ab^5 + b^6\n\\]\n\nSubstituting $a = \\sqrt{7}$ and $b = \\sqrt{5}$, we get:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{5})^6 = 7^3 + 6 \\cdot 7^{5/2} \\cdot 5^{1/2} + 15 \\cdot 7^2 \\cdot 5 + 20 \\cdot 7^{3/2} \\cdot 5^{3/2} + 15 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 5^2 + 6 \\cdot 7^{1/2} \\cdot 5^{5/2} + 5^3\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{5})^6 = 343 + 6 \\cdot 7^{5/2} \\cdot 5^{1/2} + 15 \\cdot 49 \\cdot 5 + 20 \\cdot 7^{3/2} \\cdot 5^{3/2} + 15 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 25 + 6 \\cdot 7^{1/2} \\cdot 5^{5/2} + 125\n\\]\n\nWe can calculate each term separately:\n\n\\[\n6 \\cdot 7^{5/2} \\cdot 5^{1/2} = 6 \\cdot 7^2 \\cdot \\sqrt{7} \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 6 \\cdot 49 \\cdot \\sqrt{35} = 294 \\sqrt{35}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n20 \\cdot 7^{3/2} \\cdot 5^{3/2} = 20 \\cdot 7 \\cdot \\sqrt{7} \\cdot 5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 20 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 5 \\cdot \\sqrt{35} = 700 \\sqrt{35}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n6 \\cdot 7^{1/2} \\cdot 5^{5/2} = 6 \\cdot \\sqrt{7} \\cdot 5^2 \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 6 \\cdot 25 \\cdot \\sqrt{35} = 150 \\sqrt{35}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{5})^6 = 343 + 294 \\sqrt{35} + 15 \\cdot 245 + 700 \\sqrt{35} + 15 \\cdot 175 + 150 \\sqrt{35} + 125\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{5})^6 = 343 + 15 \\cdot 245 + 15 \\cdot 175 + 125 + (294 + 700 + 150) \\sqrt{35}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{5})^6 = 343 + 3675 + 2625 + 125 + 1144 \\sqrt{35} = 6768 + 1144 \\sqrt{35}\n\\]\n\nNow we need to find the greatest integer less than $6768 + 1144 \\sqrt{35}$. We know that $\\sqrt{35}$ is approximately 5.916, so $1144 \\sqrt{35}$ is approximately $1144 \\cdot 5.916 = 6768.224$. Therefore, $6768 + 1144 \\sqrt{35}$ is approximately $6768 + 6768.224 = 13536.224$. The greatest integer less than this value is 13536.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the value of (sqrt(7) + sqrt(5))^6\na = math.sqrt(7)\nb = math.sqrt(5)\nvalue = (a + b)**6\n\n# Fin