in x\\) and \\(\\cos x\\) is \\(\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x \\cdot \\sin x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x}\n   \\]\n\n6. Recall the Pythagorean identity: \\(1 - \\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x\\). So the expression simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x\n   \\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is \\(\\cot x\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, sec, sin, cos, simplify, cot\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nexpression = sec(x) / sin(x) - sin(x) / cos(x)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = simplify(expression)\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n1/tan(x)\n```\nThe simplified expression is \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan x}\\), which is equivalent to \\(\\cot x\\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\cot x}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Recall the trigonometric identities:\n   - \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\)\n   - \\(\\tan x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\)\n\n2. Substitute these identities into the expression:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\tan x\n   \\]\n   So the expression becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\tan x\n   \\]\n\n3. To combine these terms, we need a common denominator. Recall that \\(\\tan x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), so we can rewrite the expression as:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x} = \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x}\n   \\]\n\n4. Using the Pythagorean identity \\(\\cos^2 x = 1 - \\sin^2 x\\), w