fy the expression\nsimplified_expr = sp.simplify(expr)\nprint(simplified_expr)\n```", "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), we need to express it in terms of basic trigonometric functions and simplify step-by-step.\n\n1. Recall that \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\). So, we can rewrite the first term as:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x}.\n   \\]\n\n2. The second term is \\(\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), which is the same as \\(\\tan x\\).\n\n3. Now we can rewrite the entire expression as:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\tan x.\n   \\]\n\n4. Since \\(\\tan x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), we can rewrite the expression as:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n   \\]\n\n5. To combine these terms, we need a common denominator. The common denominator for \\(\\cos x \\sin x\\) and \\(\\cos x\\) is \\(\\cos x \\sin x\\). So we rewrite the second term with this denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x}.\n   \\]\n\n6. Now we can combine the terms:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x}.\n   \\]\n\n7. Using the Pythagorean identity, \\(1 - \\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x\\), we can simplify the numerator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x.\n   \\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is \\(\\cot x\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, sec, sin, cos, simplify, cot\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nexpression = sec(x) / sin(x) - sin(x) / cos(x)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = simplify(expression)\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n1/tan(x)\n```\nThe simplified expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\) is indeed \\(\\cot x\\), which is equivalent to \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan 