\\text{Number of hats}) \\]\n\nIn this case, the calculation is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total outfits} = 5 \\times 6 \\times 8 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of shirts, pants, and hats\nnum_shirts = 5\nnum_pants = 6\nnum_hats = 8\n\n# Total number of outfits\ntotal_outfits = num_shirts * num_pants * num_hats\nprint(total_outfits)\n```\n```output\n240\n```\nThe total number of outfits that can be made consisting of one shirt, one pair of pants, and one hat is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).", "To determine the total number of possible outfits that can be made from 5 shirts, 6 pairs of pants, and 8 hats, we can use the fundamental counting principle. The fundamental counting principle states that if there are \\(m\\) ways to do one thing, \\(n\\) ways to do another, and \\(p\\) ways to do a third thing, then there are \\(m \\times n \\times p\\) ways to do all three.\n\nIn this case:\n- There are 5 ways to choose a shirt.\n- There are 6 ways to choose a pair of pants.\n- There are 8 ways to choose a hat.\n\nSo, the total number of outfits is \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 8\\).\n\nLet's calculate this using Python code.\n```python\n# Number of shirts, pants, and hats\nnum_shirts = 5\nnum_pants = 6\nnum_hats = 8\n\n# Total number of outfits\ntotal_outfits = num_shirts * num_pants * num_hats\nprint(total_outfits)\n```\n```output\n240\n```\nThe total number of possible outfits that can be made consisting of one shirt, one pair of pants, and one hat is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).", "To determine the total number of possible outfits that can be made from 5 shirts, 6 pairs of pants, and 8 hats, we can use the fundamental counting principle. The fundamental counting principle states that if there are \\(m\\) ways to do one thing, and \\(n\\) ways to do another, then there are \\(m \\times n\\) ways to do both.\n\nIn this case, we have:\n- 5 choices for shirts\n- 6 choices for pairs of pants\n- 8 choices for hats\n\nTo find the total number of possible outfits, 