minimum possible value of the expression \\(1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6\\) by adding parentheses is \\(\\boxed{-18}\\).', 'To solve this problem, we need to explore all possible ways of adding parentheses to the expression \\(1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6\\) and calculate the resulting values. We will then determine the minimum possible value.\n\nLet\'s break down the problem into smaller steps:\n\n1. Identify all possible ways to add parentheses to the expression.\n2. Evaluate each expression to find its value.\n3. Determine the minimum value among all the evaluated expressions.\n\nWe will use Python to automate this process. We\'ll consider different placements of parentheses and evaluate each expression to find the minimum value.\n\nHere\'s the Python code to solve the problem:\n\n```python\nimport itertools\n\n# Define the expression as a string\nexpression = "1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6"\n\n# Define all possible ways to add parentheses\n# We can add parentheses in different places, but we need to ensure we don\'t change the order of the terms\n# Possible placements: (1 + 2) + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6, 1 + (2 + 3) - 4 + 5 + 6, 1 + 2 + (3 - 4) + 5 + 6, etc.\n# We need to consider all combinations of parentheses placements\n\n# Generate all possible placements of parentheses\ndef generate_parentheses(expression):\n    tokens = expression.split()\n    n = len(tokens)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n+1):\n            left_expr = "({})".format(" + ".join(tokens[:i]))\n            right_expr = " + ".join(tokens[i:j]) + " + ".join(tokens[j:])\n            yield left_expr + right_expr\n\n# Evaluate each expression and find the minimum value\ndef evaluate_expression(expr):\n    return eval(expr)\n\n# Generate all possible expressions with parentheses\npossible_expressions = set()\nfor placement in generate_parentheses(expression):\n    possible_expressions.add(placement)\n\n# Evaluate each expression and find the minimum value\nmin_value = float("inf")\nfor expr in possible_expressions:\n    value = evaluate_expression(expr)\n    if value < min_value:\n        min_value = value\n\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe minimum possible value of the expression \\(1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6\\) when parentheses are added in various locations is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).', 'To solve this problem, we need to explore all possible ways of adding parentheses to the expression \\(1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6\\) and evaluate the resulting expressions. We need to find the minimum possible value of the expression when parentheses are added.\n\nLet\'s break down the problem step-by-step:\n\n1. **Identify all possible ways to add parentheses:**\n   - We can add parentheses around the entire expression, but that doesn\'t change the value.\n   - We can add parentheses around the first two terms, the first three terms, the first four terms, and so on.\n   - We need to consider all combinations of adding parentheses around sub-expressions.\n\n2. **Evaluate each possible expression:**\n   - We will evaluate each possible expression and keep track of the minimum value.\n\nLet\'s implement this in Python using the `sympy` library to handle the expressions.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\n# Define the expression as a string\nexpression = "1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6"\n\n# Function to evaluate the expression with parentheses added\ndef evaluate_expression(expr):\n    return eval(expr)\n\n# Generate all possible ways to add parentheses\ndef generate_parentheses(expr):\n    stack = []\n    for i, char in enumerate(expr):\n        if char == \'+\':\n            stack.append(\')\')\n        elif char == \'-\':\n            stack.append(\')\')\n        elif char == \'*\':\n            stack.append(\')\')\n        elif char == \'/\':\n            stack.append(\')\')\n        else:\n            stack.append(char)\n    return stack\n\n# Find all possible ways to add parentheses\ndef find_min_value(expr):\n    min_value = float(\'inf\')\n    for i 