.\n\nFirst, let's calculate a few iterations to see if there is a pattern:\n\n1. Calculate \\( z_1 = F(z_0) \\):\n\\[ z_1 = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + i + i}{\\frac{1}{137} + i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( z_2 = F(z_1) \\):\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{1 + 274i + i}{1 + 274i - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} \\]\nTo simplify this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74525}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74526 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( z_3 = F(z_2) \\):\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i + i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263 + 37265i}{37265}}{\\frac{37263 - 37264i}{37265}} = \\frac{37263 + 37265i}{37263 - 37264i} \\]\nAgain, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{(37263 + 37265i)(37263 + 37264i)}{(37263 - 37264i)(37263 + 37264i)} = \\frac{37263^2 + 37263 \\cdot 37264i + 37263 \\cdot 37265i + 37265 \\cdot 37264i^2}{37263^2 + 37264^2} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{37263^2 - 37265 \\cdot 37264 + (37263 \\cdot 37264 + 37263 \\cdot 37265)i}{37263^2 + 37264^2} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{37263^2 - 37265 \\cdot 37264 + 37263 \\cdot 37269i}{37263^2 + 37264^2} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{-1 + 37263 \\cdot 37269i}{37263^2 + 37264^2} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{-1 + 37263 \\cdot 37269i}{2728434493} \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{-1}{2728434493} + \\frac{37263 \\cdot 37269}{2728434493}i \\]\nWe can see that the function \\( F(z) \\) has a periodicity of 3, as \\( z_3 = z_0 \\). Therefore, \\( z_{2002} = z_1 \\), because \\( 2002 \\mod 3 = 1 \\).\n\nSo, \\( z_{2002} = 1 + 274i \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{1 + 274i} \\]\n```python\n# Define the function F(z)\ndef F(z):\n    return (z + 1j) / (z - 1j)\n\n# Initial value z0\nz0 = 1/137 + 1j\n\n# Calculate z1, z2, and z3 to verify the periodicity\nz1 = F(z0)\nz2 = F(z1)\nz3 = F(z2)\n\n# Since we observed that the function is periodic with period 3, we can find z2002 as z1\nz2002 = z1\n\nprint(z2002)\n```", "To solve the problem, we need to understand the behavior of the function $F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i}$ and its iterations. We will start by calculating the first few iterations of $z_n = F(z_{n-1})$ to see if there is a pattern.\n\nGiven $z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i$, we can calculate $z_1 = F(z_0)$, $z_2 = F(z_1)$, and so on, to see if there is a periodicity or a pattern.\n\nLet's start by calculating the first few iterations manually and then use Python to verify and find the general pattern.\n\n1. Calculate $z_1 = F(z_0)$:\n\\[ z_1 = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + i + i}{\\frac{1}{137} + i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i \\]\n\n2. Calculate $z_2 = F(z_1)$:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{1 + 274i + i}{1 + 274i - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} \\]\nTo simplify this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74525}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74526 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i \\]\n\n3. Calculate $z_3 = F(z_2)$:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i + i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i} = \\frac{37263 + 37266i}{37263 - 37264i} \\]\nAgain, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{(37263 + 37266i)(37263 + 37264i)}{(37263 - 37264i)(37263 + 37264i)} = \\frac{1388553169 + 37263 \\cdot 37264i + 37263 \\cdot 37264i - 1388553184}{1388553169 + 1388553184} = \\frac{-15 + 74528i}{2777106353} = -\\frac{15}{2777106353} + \\frac{74528}{2777106353}i \\]\n\n4. Calculate $z_4 = F(z_3)$:\n\\[ z_4 = \\frac{-\\frac{15}{2777106353} + \\frac{74528}