es the following steps:\n\n1. Divide the number by 5.\n2. Record the remainder.\n3. Update the number to the quotient from the division.\n4. Repeat steps 1-3 until the quotient is 0.\n5. The base 5 number is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s convert $555_{10}$ to base 5 using Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_5(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    base_5_number = ""\n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 5\n        base_5_number = str(remainder) + base_5_number\n        n = n // 5\n    \n    return base_5_number\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase_5_number = decimal_to_base_5(decimal_number)\nprint(base_5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe decimal number $555_{10}$ expressed in base 5 is $\\boxed{4210_5}$.', 'To convert a decimal number to a different base, we repeatedly divide the number by the base and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, give the number in the new base. Let\'s convert 555 from base 10 to base 5 using this method.\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, which gives 111 with a remainder of 0.\n2. Divide 111 by 5, which gives 22 with a remainder of 1.\n3. Divide 22 by 5, which gives 4 with a remainder of 2.\n4. Divide 4 by 5, which gives 0 with a remainder of 4.\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base 5 representation of 555 as $4210_5$.\n\nLet\'s verify this using Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base 5 representation of the decimal number 555 is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert the decimal number $555_{10}$ to base $5$, we nee