rstanding the Geometry:**\n   - The internal angle of a regular heptagon is given by \\( \\frac{(7-2) \\cdot 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{5 \\cdot 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\).\n   - The internal angle of a square is \\( 90^\\circ \\).\n   - Since the square and the heptagon share a common side \\( \\overline{AD} \\), the angle \\( \\angle BAD \\) is the internal angle of the heptagon minus the internal angle of the square.\n\n2. **Calculating the Angle \\( \\angle BAD \\):**\n   - The angle \\( \\angle BAD \\) is \\( \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} - 90^\\circ \\).\n   - Simplifying, we get \\( \\angle BAD = \\frac{900^\\circ - 630^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{270^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\n3. **Finding \\( \\angle BAC \\):**\n   - Since \\( \\angle BAC \\) is half of \\( \\angle BAD \\) (because \\( \\angle BAC \\) is formed by bisecting \\( \\angle BAD \\) with the side \\( \\overline{AD} \\) of the square), we have \\( \\angle BAC = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{270^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{135^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\nThe final answer is \\( \\frac{135}{7} \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculate the internal angle of the heptagon\ninternal_angle_heptagon = (7 - 2) * 180 / 7\n\n# Internal angle of the square\ninternal_angle_square = 90\n\n# Calculate the angle BAD\nangle_BAD = internal_angle_heptagon - internal_angle_square\n\n# Calculate the angle BAC\nangle_BAC = angle_BAD / 2\n\n# Display the result as a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nangle_BAC_fraction = Fraction(angle_BAC).limit_denominator()\nprint(angle_BAC_fraction)\n```\n```output\n135/7\n```\nThe degree measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{135}{7}}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) given that a square and a regular heptagon share a common side \\(\\overline{AD}\\).\n\n1. **Understand the Geometry:**\n   - A square has interior angles of \\(90^\\circ\\).\n   - A regular heptagon has interior angles of \\(