\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ g & h & i \\end{pmatrix}$. Then we have:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3a + b \\\\ 3d + e \\\\ 3g + h \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -5a + 2b + 2c \\\\ -5d + 2e + 2f \\\\ -5g + 2h + 2i \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nThis gives us the following system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n3a + b = 2 \\\\\n3d + e = 4 \\\\\n3g + h = -3 \\\\\n-5a + 2b + 2c = 0 \\\\\n-5d + 2e + 2f = -5 \\\\\n-5g + 2h + 2i = -5\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nWe need to solve this system to find the values of $a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h,$ and $i$. Once we have these values, we can find $\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$. Let's solve the system using Python.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variables\r\na, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i = symbols('a b c d e f g h i')\r\n\r\n# Define the equations based on the given information\r\neq1 = Eq(3*a + b, 2)\r\neq2 = Eq(3*d + e, 4)\r\neq3 = Eq(3*g + h, -3)\r\neq4 = Eq(-5*a + 2*b + 2*c, 0)\r\neq5 = Eq(-5*d + 2*e + 2*f, -5)\r\neq6 = Eq(-5*g + 2*h + 2*i, -5)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4, eq5, eq6), (a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i))\r\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n{a: 2/11 - 2*c/11, b: 4*c/11 + 20/11, d: 2*f/5 - 1/5, e: 14/5 - 2*f/5, g: 2*i/5 - 1/5, h: -2*i/5 - 13/5}\n```\nThe solution to the system of equations gives us the following relationships:\n\\[\na = \\frac{2}{11} - \\frac{2c}{11}, \\quad b = \\frac{4c}{11} + \\frac{20}{11}, \\quad d = \\frac{2f}{5} - \\frac{1}{5}, \\quad e = \\frac{14}{5} - \\frac{2f}{5}, \\quad g = \\frac{2i}{5} - \\frac{1}{5}, \\quad h = -\\frac{2i}{5} - \\frac{13}{5}.\n\\]\nWe can choose specific values for $c$, $f$, and $i$ to determine the matrix $\\