 sum of \\(m\\angle J\\) and \\(m\\angle H\\) is \\(180\\) degrees. Let's confirm this with a simple Python code using sympy to ensure the calculation is correct.\n\n```python\n# Since we are just confirming a geometric property, we don't need complex calculations.\n# We can simply print the result based on the geometric reasoning.\n\n# Sum of angles in a quadrilateral is 360 degrees\n# Two right angles (90 degrees each) from the tangents\n# Therefore, the sum of the remaining two angles is 360 - 180 = 180 degrees\n\nsum_of_angles = 360 - (90 + 90)\nprint(sum_of_angles)\n```\n```output\n180\n```\nThe sum of \\(m\\angle J\\) and \\(m\\angle H\\) is \\(\\boxed{180}\\) degrees.", "To find the remainder when the sum of the first 10 positive integers is divided by 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the sum of the first 10 positive integers.\n2. Find the remainder when this sum is divided by 9.\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) positive integers is given by the formula:\n\\[ S = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} \\]\nFor \\( n = 10 \\):\n\\[ S = \\frac{10 \\cdot 11}{2} = 55 \\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 55 is divided by 9. This can be done using the modulus operation.\n\nLet's calculate this using Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the sum of the first 10 positive integers\nn = 10\nsum_of_integers = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n# Find the remainder when the sum is divided by 9\nremainder = sum_of_integers % 9\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe remainder when the sum of the first 10 positive integers (which is 55) is divided by 9 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).", "To find the remainder when the sum of the first 10 positive integers is divided by 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the sum of the first 10 positive integers.\n2. Find the remainder when this sum is divided by 9.\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) positive integers is given by the formula:\n\\[ S = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} \\]\nFor \\( n = 10 \\):\n\\[ S = \\frac{10 \\cdot 11}{2} = 55 \\]\nNow, we ne