th Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Total number of medals\nn = 4\n# Frequency of IMO gold medals\nfreq_imo = 2\n# Frequency of IPhO gold medals\nfreq_ipho = 2\n\n# Calculate the number of distinct arrangements\ndistinct_arrangements = math.factorial(n) // (math.factorial(freq_imo) * math.factorial(freq_ipho))\nprint(distinct_arrangements)\n```\n```output\n6\n```\nThe number of distinct arrangements of 2 IMO gold medals and 2 IPhO gold medals is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).", "Since the IMO gold medals are indistinguishable, and the IPhO gold medals are indistinguishable, we can treat each set of medals as a single entity. Therefore, we need to find the number of ways to arrange these two entities in a row.\n\nThe number of ways to arrange \\( n \\) distinct objects is given by \\( n! \\) (n factorial), which is the product of all positive integers up to \\( n \\). In this case, we have 2 entities (the IMO gold medals and the IPhO gold medals), so the number of distinct arrangements is \\( 2! = 2 \\times 1 = 2 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Number of distinct entities (IMO and IPhO medals)\nn = 2\n\n# Calculate the number of distinct arrangements\nnum_arrangements = math.factorial(n)\nprint(num_arrangements)\n```\n```output\n2\n```\nThe number of distinct arrangements of the 2 indistinguishable IMO gold medals and 2 indistinguishable IPhO gold medals in a row is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of distinct arrangements of 2 indistinguishable IMO gold medals and 2 indistinguishable IPhO gold medals. This is a combinatorial problem that can be solved using the formula for permutations of a multiset.\n\nThe formula for the number of distinct permutations of a multiset is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{n!}{n_1! \\cdot n_2! \\cdot \\ldots \\cdot n_k!}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(n\\) is the total number of items to arrange, and \\(n_1, n_2, \\ldots, n_k\\) are the frequencies of the distinct items.\n\nIn 