e total cost for Pam and the total cost for Susan, which is \\(70 - 60 = 10\\) dollars.\n\nLet's implement this in Python to verify the calculations.\n```python\n# Constants\nfull_price = 20\nsusan_discount = 0.25\npam_discount = 0.30\nsusan_tickets = 4\npam_tickets = 5\n\n# Calculate the price per ticket after discount\nsusan_price_per_ticket = full_price * (1 - susan_discount)\npam_price_per_ticket = full_price * (1 - pam_discount)\n\n# Calculate the total cost for Susan and Pam\nsusan_total_cost = susan_tickets * susan_price_per_ticket\npam_total_cost = pam_tickets * pam_price_per_ticket\n\n# Calculate the difference in cost\ncost_difference = pam_total_cost - susan_total_cost\nprint(cost_difference)\n```\n```output\n10.0\n```\nThe difference in the amount paid by Pam and Susan is \\(\\boxed{10}\\) dollars.", "First, we need to calculate the total cost for Susan and Pam after applying their respective discounts.\n\nSusan buys 4 tickets with a 25% discount:\n- The full price for 4 tickets is \\(4 \\times 20 = 80\\) dollars.\n- The discount is \\(25\\% \\times 80 = 0.25 \\times 80 = 20\\) dollars.\n- So, the total cost for Susan is \\(80 - 20 = 60\\) dollars.\n\nPam buys 5 tickets with a 30% discount:\n- The full price for 5 tickets is \\(5 \\times 20 = 100\\) dollars.\n- The discount is \\(30\\% \\times 100 = 0.30 \\times 100 = 30\\) dollars.\n- So, the total cost for Pam is \\(100 - 30 = 70\\) dollars.\n\nNow, we need to find out how many more dollars Pam pays than Susan:\n\\[ \\text{Difference} = 70 - 60 = 10 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the full price of one ticket\nticket_price = 20\n\n# Calculate the total cost for Susan\nsusan_tickets = 4\nsusan_discount = 0.25\nsusan_total_cost = susan_tickets * ticket_price * (1 - susan_discount)\n\n# Calculate the total cost for Pam\npam_tickets = 5\npam_discount = 0.30\npam_total_cost = pam_tickets * ticket_price * (1 - pam_discount)\n\n# Calculate the difference in co