 function \\( f(x) = 2x - 3 \\).\n2. Subtract 1 from the result of \\( f(5) \\).\n3. Use the result from step 2 as the input to the function \\( g(x) = x + 1 \\) to find \\( g(f(5) - 1) \\).\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step and implement it in Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we calculate \\( f(5) \\):\n\\[ f(5) = 2(5) - 3 = 10 - 3 = 7 \\]\n\nNext, we subtract 1 from \\( f(5) \\):\n\\[ f(5) - 1 = 7 - 1 = 6 \\]\n\nFinally, we use this result as the input to the function \\( g(x) \\):\n\\[ g(6) = 6 + 1 = 7 \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( g(f(5) - 1) \\) is 7. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the functions f and g\ndef f(x):\n    return 2 * x - 3\n\ndef g(x):\n    return x + 1\n\n# Calculate f(5)\nf_5 = f(5)\n\n# Calculate f(5) - 1\nf_5_minus_1 = f_5 - 1\n\n# Calculate g(f(5) - 1)\nresult = g(f_5_minus_1)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n7\n```\nThe value of \\( g(f(5) - 1) \\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the value of \\( f(5) \\).\n2. Subtract 1 from the value obtained in step 1.\n3. Use the result from step 2 as the input to the function \\( g(x) \\).\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n1. Calculate \\( f(5) \\):\n\\[ f(x) = 2x - 3 \\]\n\\[ f(5) = 2(5) - 3 = 10 - 3 = 7 \\]\n\n2. Subtract 1 from \\( f(5) \\):\n\\[ 7 - 1 = 6 \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( g(6) \\):\n\\[ g(x) = x + 1 \\]\n\\[ g(6) = 6 + 1 = 7 \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( g(f(5) - 1) \\) is \\( 7 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the functions f and g\ndef f(x):\n    return 2 * x - 3\n\ndef g(x):\n    return x + 1\n\n# Calculate f(5)\nf_5 = f(5)\n\n# Calculate f(5) - 1\nf_5_minus_1 = f_5 - 1\n\n# Calculate g(f(5) - 1)\nresult = g(f_5_minus_1)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n7\n```\nThe value of \\( g(f(5) - 1) \\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).", 'First, we need to find the value of $f(5)$. Substituting $x=5$ into the function $f(x) = 2x-3$, we get:\n\\[f(5) = 2(5) - 3 = 10 - 3 = 7\\]\n\nNext, we need to find