atest possible value for the largest of the three integers in the set is \\(\\boxed{58}\\).", "Let's denote the three consecutive integers as \\(n-1\\), \\(n\\), and \\(n+1\\). The sum of these integers is \\((n-1) + n + (n+1) = 3n\\). We need to find the greatest possible value of \\(n+1\\) such that \\(3n\\) is a three-digit palindrome and less than 220. \n\nA three-digit palindrome has the form \\(aba\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are digits. This can be expressed as \\(100a + 10b + a = 101a + 10b\\). Since \\(3n < 220\\), the possible values for \\(3n\\) are three-digit palindromes less than 220. The three-digit palindromes less than 220 are 101, 111, 121, 131, 141, 151, 161, 171, 181, and 191. We need to check which of these values can be expressed as \\(3n\\).\n\nLet's check each palindrome:\n- \\(101 \\div 3 = 33.67\\) (not an integer)\n- \\(111 \\div 3 = 37\\) (integer, so \\(n = 37\\), and \\(n+1 = 38\\))\n- \\(121 \\div 3 = 40.33\\) (not an integer)\n- \\(131 \\div 3 = 43.67\\) (not an integer)\n- \\(141 \\div 3 = 47\\) (integer, so \\(n = 47\\), and \\(n+1 = 48\\))\n- \\(151 \\div 3 = 50.33\\) (not an integer)\n- \\(161 \\div 3 = 53.67\\) (not an integer)\n- \\(171 \\div 3 = 57\\) (integer, so \\(n = 57\\), and \\(n+1 = 58\\))\n- \\(181 \\div 3 = 60.33\\) (not an integer)\n- \\(191 \\div 3 = 63.67\\) (not an integer)\n\nThe greatest possible value for \\(n+1\\) is 58. Let's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# List of three-digit palindromes less than 220\npalindromes = [101, 111, 121, 131, 141, 151, 161, 171, 181, 191]\n\n# Find the greatest possible value for the largest integer in the set\nmax_largest_integer = 0\nfor palindrome in palindromes:\n    if palindrome % 3 == 0:\n        n = palindrome // 3\n        largest_integer = n + 1\n        if largest_integer > max_largest_integer:\n            max_largest_integer = largest_integer\n\nprint(max_largest_integer)\n```\n```output\n58\n```\nThe greatest possible value for the la