hich is a quadratic polynomial.\n3. The third term is \\(\\frac{(x - a)(x - b)}{(c - a)(c - b)}\\). The numerator \\((x - a)(x - b)\\) expands to \\(x^2 - (a+b)x + ab\\), which is a quadratic polynomial.\n\nSince each term is a fraction with a quadratic polynomial in the numerator, the degree of each term is 2. When we add these terms together, the resulting polynomial will have a degree of at most 2. To confirm this, let's evaluate \\(p(x)\\) at specific points.\n\nWe can evaluate \\(p(x)\\) at \\(x = a\\), \\(x = b\\), and \\(x = c\\):\n\n- When \\(x = a\\), the first term becomes \\(\\frac{(a - b)(a - c)}{(a - b)(a - c)} = 1\\), the second term becomes \\(\\frac{(a - a)(a - c)}{(b - a)(b - c)} = 0\\), and the third term becomes \\(\\frac{(a - a)(a - b)}{(c - a)(c - b)} = 0\\). So, \\(p(a) = 1 + 0 + 0 = 1\\).\n- When \\(x = b\\), the first term becomes \\(\\frac{(b - b)(b - c)}{(a - b)(a - c)} = 0\\), the second term becomes \\(\\frac{(b - a)(b - c)}{(b - a)(b - c)} = 1\\), and the third term becomes \\(\\frac{(b - a)(b - b)}{(c - a)(c - b)} = 0\\). So, \\(p(b) = 0 + 1 + 0 = 1\\).\n- When \\(x = c\\), the first term becomes \\(\\frac{(c - b)(c - c)}{(a - b)(a - c)} = 0\\), the second term becomes \\(\\frac{(c - a)(c - c)}{(b - a)(b - c)} = 0\\), and the third term becomes \\(\\frac{(c - a)(c - b)}{(c - a)(c - b)} = 1\\). So, \\(p(c) = 0 + 0 + 1 = 1\\).\n\nSince \\(p(a) = 1\\), \\(p(b) = 1\\), and \\(p(c) = 1\\), we see that \\(p(x) = 1\\) for \\(x = a, b, c\\). This means that \\(p(x) - 1\\) has roots at \\(x = a, b, c\\). Therefore, \\(p(x) - 1 = k(x - a)(x - b)(x - c)\\) for some constant \\(k\\). However, since \\(p(x)\\) is a polynomial of degree at most 2, \\(k\\) must be 0, and thus \\(p(x) = 1\\).\n\nTherefore, the degree of the polynomial \\(p(x)\\) is 0. Let's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, simplify\r\n\r\n# Define the variables\r\nx, a, b, c = symbols('x a b c')\r\n\r\n# Define the polynomial p(x)\r\np_x = ((x - b)