s_for_hallway\nprint(length_of_hallway)\n```\n```output\n10.0\n```\nThe length of the hallway is \\(\\boxed{10}\\) meters.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the speed of the robot and then use that speed to find the length of the hallway.\n\n1. First, we calculate the speed of the robot. The robot takes 2.5 hours to travel 1 kilometer. Since speed is distance divided by time, we can calculate the speed in kilometers per hour:\n\\[ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{1 \\text{ km}}{2.5 \\text{ hours}} = 0.4 \\text{ km/h} \\]\n\n2. Next, we need to convert the speed from kilometers per hour to meters per second because the time given for the hallway is in seconds. There are 1000 meters in a kilometer and 3600 seconds in an hour, so:\n\\[ 0.4 \\text{ km/h} = 0.4 \\times \\frac{1000 \\text{ m}}{3600 \\text{ s}} = \\frac{0.4 \\times 1000}{3600} \\text{ m/s} = \\frac{400}{3600} \\text{ m/s} = \\frac{1}{9} \\text{ m/s} \\]\n\n3. The robot takes 90 seconds to travel the length of the hallway at this speed. Therefore, the length of the hallway is:\n\\[ \\text{Length of hallway} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = \\frac{1}{9} \\text{ m/s} \\times 90 \\text{ s} = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nSo, the length of the hallway is \\( \\boxed{10} \\) meters. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the given values\ntime_to_travel_1_km = 2.5  # hours\ndistance_1_km = 1  # kilometer\ntime_to_travel_hallway = 90  # seconds\n\n# Calculate the speed in km/h\nspeed_km_per_h = distance_1_km / time_to_travel_1_km\n\n# Convert the speed to m/s\nspeed_m_per_s = speed_km_per_h * (1000 / 3600)\n\n# Calculate the length of the hallway\nlength_of_hallway = speed_m_per_s * time_to_travel_hallway\nprint(length_of_hallway)\n```", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the speed of the robot and then use that speed to find the length of the hallway.\n\n1. First, we need to find the speed of the robot. The robot takes 2.5 hours to travel 1 kilometer. We can convert 2.5 hours in