tinct prime divisors are 2, 3, 7, and 13. The sum of these distinct prime divisors is:\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 7 + 13 = 25\n\\]\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{25}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Find all the positive divisors of 500.\n2. Calculate the sum of these divisors.\n3. Determine the distinct prime divisors of this sum.\n4. Calculate the sum of these distinct prime divisors.\n\nFirst, let's find all the positive divisors of 500. The prime factorization of 500 is \\(500 = 2^2 \\times 5^3\\). The sum of the divisors of a number \\(n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k}\\) is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\sigma(n) = (1 + p_1 + p_1^2 + \\cdots + p_1^{e_1})(1 + p_2 + p_2^2 + \\cdots + p_2^{e_2}) \\cdots (1 + p_k + p_k^2 + \\cdots + p_k^{e_k})\n\\]\nFor \\(500 = 2^2 \\times 5^3\\), the sum of the divisors is:\n\\[\n\\sigma(500) = (1 + 2 + 2^2)(1 + 5 + 5^2 + 5^3) = (1 + 2 + 4)(1 + 5 + 25 + 125) = 7 \\times 156 = 1092\n\\]\nNext, we need to find the distinct prime divisors of 1092. We start by finding the prime factorization of 1092. We can do this by dividing 1092 by the smallest prime number, 2, and continuing with the quotient until we can't divide by 2 anymore, then moving on to the next smallest prime number, and so on.\n\nLet's factorize 1092:\n\\[\n1092 \\div 2 = 546 \\quad \\text{(1092 is divisible by 2)}\n\\]\n\\[\n546 \\div 2 = 273 \\quad \\text{(546 is divisible by 2)}\n\\]\n\\[\n273 \\div 3 = 91 \\quad \\text{(273 is divisible by 3)}\n\\]\n\\[\n91 \\div 7 = 13 \\quad \\text{(91 is divisible by 7)}\n\\]\n\\[\n13 \\div 13 = 1 \\quad \\text{(13 is divisible by 13)}\n\\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 1092 is \\(1092 = 2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7 \\times 13\\). The distinct prime divisors are 2, 3, 7, and 13. The sum of these distinct prime divisors is:\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 7 + 13 = 25\n\\]\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport sympy\n\n# Find the sum of the divisors of 500\nn = 