tand the Inequality:**\n   The inequality \\(|x - 2| \\leq 5.6\\) means that the distance between \\(x\\) and 2 on the number line is less than or equal to 5.6. This can be rewritten as:\n   \\[\n   -5.6 \\leq x - 2 \\leq 5.6\n   \\]\n   Adding 2 to all parts of the inequality, we get:\n   \\[\n   -5.6 + 2 \\leq x \\leq 5.6 + 2\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   -3.6 \\leq x \\leq 7.6\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the Integer Solutions:**\n   The integers that lie between -3.6 and 7.6 are -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7. So, there are 11 integers in this range.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the range of x\nlower_bound = -3.6\nupper_bound = 7.6\n\n# Find all integers in the range [lower_bound, upper_bound]\ninteger_solutions = [x for x in range(int(lower_bound), int(upper_bound) + 1) if lower_bound <= x <= upper_bound]\n\n# The number of integers in the solution set\nnum_integer_solutions = len(integer_solutions)\nprint((num_integer_solutions, integer_solutions))\n```\n```output\n(11, [-3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7])\n```\nThe number of integers in the solution set of \\(|x - 2| \\leq 5.6\\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).", "To determine the number of integers in the solution set of \\(|x-2| \\leq 5.6\\), we first need to solve the inequality.\n\nThe inequality \\(|x-2| \\leq 5.6\\) can be split into two separate inequalities:\n1. \\(x - 2 \\leq 5.6\\)\n2. \\(-(x - 2) \\leq 5.6\\)\n\nLet's solve these inequalities one by one.\n\n1. \\(x - 2 \\leq 5.6\\)\n\\[x \\leq 7.6\\]\n\n2. \\(-(x - 2) \\leq 5.6\\)\n\\[ -x + 2 \\leq 5.6\\]\n\\[ -x \\leq 3.6\\]\n\\[ x \\geq -3.6\\]\n\nCombining these two inequalities, we get:\n\\[ -3.6 \\leq x \\leq 7.6\\]\n\nThe integers that satisfy this inequality are \\(-3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\\). \n\nSo, the number of integers in the solution set is \\(11\\).\n\nLet's write the Python code to confirm this:\n\n```python\n# Define the range of the inequality\nlower_bound = -3.6\nupper_bound 