ve the normal equations \\( A^T A \\mathbf{x} = A^T \\mathbf{b} \\), where \\( A \\) is the given matrix and \\( \\mathbf{b} \\) is the given vector.\n\nFirst, we compute \\( A^T \\):\n\\[ A^T = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccccc}\n-2 & 3 & 3 & 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\\n-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\\n-3 & -3 & -2 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\\n2 & 2 & -3 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right) \\]\n\nNext, we compute \\( A^T A \\):\n\\[ A^T A = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n42 & 0 & -12 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 20 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n-12 & 0 & 34 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 0 & 0 & 20 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right) \\]\n\nThen, we compute \\( A^T \\mathbf{b} \\):\n\\[ A^T \\mathbf{b} = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n-1.67 \\\\\n-1.97 \\\\\n-1.67 \\\\\n-1.97 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right) \\]\n\nNow, we solve the system \\( A^T A \\mathbf{x} = A^T \\mathbf{b} \\):\n\\[ \\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n42 & 0 & -12 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 20 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n-12 & 0 & 34 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 0 & 0 & 20 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right) \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\nx_1 \\\\\nx_2 \\\\\nx_3 \\\\\nx_4 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right) = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n-1.67 \\\\\n-1.97 \\\\\n-1.67 \\\\\n-1.97 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right) \\]\n\nThis gives us the following system of equations:\n\\[ 42x_1 - 12x_3 = -1.67 \\]\n\\[ 20x_2 = -1.97 \\]\n\\[ -12x_1 + 34x_3 = -1.67 \\]\n\\[ 20x_4 = -1.97 \\]\n\nSolving these equations, we get:\n\\[ x_2 = \\frac{-1.97}{20} = -0.0985 \\]\n\\[ x_4 = \\frac{-1.97}{20} = -0.0985 \\]\n\\[ 42x_1 - 12x_3 = -1.67 \\]\n\\[ -12x_1 + 34x_3 = -1.67 \\]\n\nWe can solve the last two equations simultaneously. Multiply the first equation by 34 and the second equation by 12:\n\\[ 1428x_1 - 408x_3 = -56.78 \\]\n\\[ -144x_1 + 408x_3 = -20.04 \\]\n\nAdd these two equations:\n\\[ 1284x_1 = -76.82 \\]\n\\[ x_1 = \\frac{-76.82}{1284} = -0.0597 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( x_1 = -0.0597 \\) back into the equation \\( 42x_1 - 12x_3 = -1.67 \\):\n\\[ 42(-0.0597) - 12x_3 = -1.67 \\]\n\\[ -2.5074 - 12x_3 = -1.67 \\]\n\\[ -12x_3 = -1.67 + 2.5074 \\]\n\\[ -12x