 Python code.\n```python\n# Function to check if a number is divisible by 6\ndef is_divisible_by_6(number):\n    return number % 6 == 0\n\n# Check for each possible value of N\npossible_values = [2, 4, 6, 8]\nfor N in possible_values:\n    number = 214200 + N\n    if is_divisible_by_6(number):\n        result = N\n        break\n\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n6\n```\nThe nonzero value of \\( N \\) that makes the number \\( 21420N \\) divisible by 6 is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).", "To determine the nonzero value of \\( N \\) that makes the number \\( 21420N \\) divisible by 6, we need to check two conditions:\n\n1. The number must be divisible by 2.\n2. The number must be divisible by 3.\n\nFor a number to be divisible by 2, its units digit must be even. So \\( N \\) must be one of \\{2, 4, 6, 8\\}.\n\nFor a number to be divisible by 3, the sum of its digits must be divisible by 3. The sum of the digits of \\( 21420N \\) is \\( 2 + 1 + 4 + 2 + 0 + N = 9 + N \\). So \\( 9 + N \\) must be divisible by 3. Since 9 is already divisible by 3, \\( N \\) must also be divisible by 3. So \\( N \\) must be one of \\{3, 6, 9\\}.\n\nThe only nonzero digit that satisfies both conditions (i.e., \\( N \\) must be even and divisible by 3) is \\( N = 6 \\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Function to check if a number is divisible by 6\ndef is_divisible_by_6(number):\n    return number % 6 == 0\n\n# Iterate over possible values of N (1 to 9) and check the conditions\nfor N in range(1, 10):\n    number = 214200 + N  # Construct the number 21420N\n    if is_divisible_by_6(number):\n        result = N\n        break\n\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n6\n```\nThe nonzero value of \\( N \\) that makes the number \\( 21420N \\) divisible by 6 is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).", "To determine the value of \\( N \\) that makes the number \\( 21420N \\) divisible by 6, we need to check two conditions:\n\n1. The number must be divisible by 2.\n2. The number must be divisible by 3.\n\nFor a num