 we get:\n\\[\n\\alpha_1 + \\alpha_2 + \\alpha_3 + \\alpha_4 = -2,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_2 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = 0,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_3\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = 0,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = 2.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the unordered set \\(\\{\\alpha_1\\alpha_2 + \\alpha_3\\alpha_4, \\alpha_1\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_4, \\alpha_1\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3\\}\\). Let's denote these expressions as \\(S_1, S_2, S_3\\). We know that:\n\\[\nS_1 + S_2 + S_3 = \\alpha_1\\alpha_2 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = 0.\n\\]\n\nTo find the individual values, we can use the fact that the roots come in conjugate pairs. Let's assume \\(\\alpha_1 = a + bi\\), \\(\\alpha_2 = a - bi\\), \\(\\alpha_3 = c + di\\), and \\(\\alpha_4 = c - di\\). Then we have:\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_2 = (a + bi)(a - bi) = a^2 + b^2,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = (c + di)(c - di) = c^2 + d^2.\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_4 = (a + bi)(c + di) + (a - bi)(c - di) = ac + adi + bci - bd + ac - adi - bci - bd = 2ac - 2bd,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3 = (a + bi)(c - di) + (a - bi)(c + di) = ac - adi + bci + bd + ac + adi - bci + bd = 2ac + 2bd.\n\\]\n\nSince the sum of these expressions is zero, we have:\n\\[\na^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2 + 2ac = 0.\n\\]\n\nGiven that the polynomial is symmetric and the roots are complex, we can conclude that the expressions \\(\\alpha_1\\alpha_2 + \\alpha_3\\alpha_4\\), \\(\\alpha_1\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_4\\), and \\(\\alpha_1\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3\\) must be the roots of a simpler polynomial. By comparing the coefficients, we can see that the polynomial \\(y^3 - 4y - 4 = 0\\) has roots that are the desired expressions. Solving this polynomial, we get the