ears that \\(a_n\\) follows a pattern related to the sequence \\(A001045\\), which is the sequence of Jacobsthal numbers. The Jacobsthal numbers \\(J_n\\) are defined by the recurrence relation \\(J_n = J_{n-1} + 2J_{n-2}\\) with initial conditions \\(J_0 = 0\\) and \\(J_1 = 1\\).\n\n4. **Sum of the Sequence:**\n   Given \\(f(1) = f(1986)\\), we can use the fact that \\(f(n) = a_n - b_n f(1)\\) to find the sum \\(f(1) + f(2) + \\dots + f(1985)\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} f(n) = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (a_n - b_n f(1)) = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} a_n - f(1) \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} b_n\n   \\]\n   The sum of the Jacobsthal numbers \\(a_n\\) is known to be \\(J_{1986} - 1\\), and the sum of \\(b_n\\) is \\(2^{1985} - 1\\).\n\n5. **Final Calculation:**\n   Since \\(f(1) = f(1986)\\), we can use the recurrence relation to find \\(f(1986)\\):\n   \\[\n   f(1986) = a_{1986} - b_{1986} f(1)\n   \\]\n   Given \\(f(1) = f(1986)\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   f(1) = a_{1986} - b_{1986} f(1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(1) (1 + b_{1986}) = a_{1986}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(1) (1 + 2^{1985}) = a_{1986}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(1) = \\frac{a_{1986}}{1 + 2^{1985}}\n   \\]\n   The sum of the sequence is then:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} f(n) = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} a_n - f(1) \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} b_n\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = J_{1986} - 1 - \\frac{a_{1986}}{1 + 2^{1985}} (2^{1985} - 1)\n   \\]\n   Since \\(J_{1986} = a_{1986} + 1\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} f(n) = (a_{1986} + 1) - 1 - \\frac{a_{1986}}{1 + 2^{1985}} (2^{1985} - 1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = a_{1986} - \\frac{a_{1986} (2^{1985} - 1)}{1 + 2^{1985}}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = a_{1986} \\left(1 - \\frac{2^{1985} - 1}{1 + 2^{1985}}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = a_{1986} \\left(\\frac{1 + 2^{1985} - 2^{1985} + 1}{1 + 2^{1985}}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = a_{1986} \\left(\\frac{2}{1 + 2^{1985}}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = \\frac{2a_{1986}}{1 + 2^{1985}}\n   \\]\n   Since \\(a_{1986} = f(1) (1 + 2^{1985})\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=1}^{1985}