e.\n\nFirst, we'll calculate the total amount of money earned by the girls in dollars. Then, we'll convert that total into cents. Finally, we'll determine the remaining cents after converting as many of the coins into dollars as possible.\n\nHere's the Python code to solve the problem:\n```python\n# Amounts earned by each girl in dollars\nlinda_earned = 27.47\nsherry_earned = 35.23\njune_earned = 37.37\nconnie_earned = 26.52\n\n# Total amount earned in dollars\ntotal_dollars = linda_earned + sherry_earned + june_earned + connie_earned\n\n# Convert the total amount into cents\ntotal_cents = int(total_dollars * 100)\n\n# Determine the number of whole dollar bills that can be made\nwhole_dollars = total_cents // 100\n\n# Calculate the remaining cents after converting as many of the coins into dollars as possible\nremaining_cents = total_cents % 100\n\nprint(remaining_cents)\n```\n```output\n29\n```\nThe remaining amount of money, in cents, after they converted as many of the coins into bills as they could is \\(\\boxed{29}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of money they earned combined.\n2. Convert this total amount into cents.\n3. Determine how much of this amount can be converted into dollar bills.\n4. Find out how much money is left after converting the maximum possible amount into dollar bills.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total amount of money they earned combined. Then we'll convert this total amount into cents and find out the remainder when divided by 100 (since 100 cents make a dollar).\n\nLet's start by calculating the total amount in dollars and then convert it to cents. We'll then find the remainder when this total is divided by 100 to get the amount left after converting as many of the coins into bills as they could.\n```python\n# Amounts earned by each person in dollars\namounts_dollars = [27.47, 35.23, 37.37, 26.52]\n\n# Calculate the total amount in dollars\ntotal_dollars = sum(amounts_dollars