\nWe can simplify the fractional part \\(\\frac{2}{4}\\) to \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the final answer is:\n\n\\[ 137\\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 11 / 4  # hours (which is 2 + 3/4 hours)\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 4)  # since the denominator is 4\n\n# Simplify the fractional part\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, 4)\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // common_divisor\nsimplified_denominator = 4 // common_divisor\n\n# Output the mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number}{simplified_numerator}/{simplified_denominator}" if simplified_denominator != 1 else f"{whole_number + simplified_numerator}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n1371/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(137\\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]', 'To determine how far a car travels in $2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour, we need to multiply the speed by the time. First, we convert the mixed number $2\\frac{3}{4}$ to an improper fraction, which is $\\frac{11}{4}$. Then we multiply this by 50 miles per hour.\n\nThe calculation is as follows:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nLet\'s perform this calculation step-by-step in Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 11 / 4  # hours (as a decimal)\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_part = int(distance)\nfractional_part = distance - whole_part\nfraction_numerator = fractional_part * 4  # since the denominator is 4\n\n# Output the mixed number\nmixe