sum of 7 is:\n\n\\[ P(\\text{sum of 7}) = p \\cdot q + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot p \\]\n\\[ = pq + 4 \\cdot \\left( \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\right) + pq \\]\n\\[ = 2pq + \\frac{4}{36} \\]\n\\[ = 2pq + \\frac{1}{9} \\]\n\nWe are given that this probability is \\( \\frac{47}{288} \\):\n\n\\[ 2pq + \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( p \\) and \\( q \\), we first need to express \\( q \\) in terms of \\( p \\):\n\n\\[ q = \\frac{1}{3} - p \\]\n\nSubstituting \\( q \\) into the equation:\n\n\\[ 2p \\left( \\frac{1}{3} - p \\right) + \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{2p}{3} - 2p^2 + \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{2p}{3} - 2p^2 = \\frac{47}{288} - \\frac{1}{9} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{2p}{3} - 2p^2 = \\frac{47}{288} - \\frac{32}{288} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{2p}{3} - 2p^2 = \\frac{15}{288} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{2p}{3} - 2p^2 = \\frac{5}{96} \\]\n\\[ 64p - 192p^2 = 5 \\]\n\\[ 192p^2 - 64p + 5 = 0 \\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation. We can solve it using the quadratic formula \\( p = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 192 \\), \\( b = -64 \\), and \\( c = 5 \\):\n\n\\[ p = \\frac{64 \\pm \\sqrt{(-64)^2 - 4 \\cdot 192 \\cdot 5}}{2 \\cdot 192} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{64 \\pm \\sqrt{4096 - 3840}}{384} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{64 \\pm \\sqrt{256}}{384} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{64 \\pm 16}{384} \\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\n\\[ p = \\frac{80}{384} = \\frac{5}{24} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{48}{384} = \\frac{1}{8} \\]\n\nSince \\( p \\) must be greater than \\( \\frac{1}{6} \\), we have \\( p = \\frac{5}{24} \\). The probability of obtaining face \\( F \\) is \\( \\frac{5}{24} \\). The sum of the numerator and the denominator is \\( 5 + 24 = 29 \\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{29}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the calculations are correct.\n```python\nfrom sympy i