re the expressions inside the absolute values change are \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since \\( p < 15 \\), the point \\( x = p + 15 \\) is outside the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\).\n\nTo find the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at the critical points \\( x = p \\) and \\( x = 15 \\), and check if there is any point within the interval where the function might have a minimum value.\n\n1. Evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at \\( x = p \\):\n\\[ f(p) = |p - p| + |p - 15| + |p - p - 15| = 0 + |p - 15| + 15 = 15 + (15 - p) = 30 - p. \\]\n\n2. Evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at \\( x = 15 \\):\n\\[ f(15) = |15 - p| + |15 - 15| + |15 - p - 15| = |15 - p| + 0 + | - p| = 15 - p + p = 15. \\]\n\nSince \\( f(x) \\) is a piecewise linear function and the minimum value of a piecewise linear function on a closed interval occurs at one of the endpoints or at a point where the derivative changes (which is not applicable here since the function is not differentiable at the points where the absolute value changes), we only need to compare the values at the endpoints.\n\nComparing \\( f(p) = 30 - p \\) and \\( f(15) = 15 \\), we see that for \\( 0 < p < 15 \\), \\( 30 - p > 15 \\). Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nThus, the minimum value taken by \\( f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).', "To solve the problem, we need to find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - (p + 15)| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\).\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Understand the Function:**\n   The function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - (p + 15)| \\) consists of three absolute value terms. The critical points where the behavior of the function changes are at \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\).\n\n2. **Analyze the Function in Different Intervals:**\n   Since we are only interested in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to consider the behavior of the function within this interval. For \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the term \\( |x - p| \\) will be \\( x - p \\), the term \\( |x - 15| \\) will be \\( 15 - x \\), and the term \\( |x - (p + 15)| \\) will be \\( (p + 15) - x \\) because \\( p + 15 \\) is outside the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\).\n\n   So, for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the function simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + ((p + 15) - x) = x - p + 15 - x + p + 15 - x = 30 - x\n   \\]\n   Therefore, \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\).\n\n3. **Find the Minimum Value:**\n   The function \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\). So, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in this interval will occur at \\( x = 15 \\).\n\n   Substituting \\( x = 15 \\) into the function, we get:\n   \\[\n   f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15\n   \\]\n\nSo, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( \\boxed{15} \\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\nx, p = sp.symbols('x p')\n\n# Define the function f(x)\nf = sp.Abs(x - p) + sp.Abs(x - 15) + sp.Abs(x - (p + 15))\n\n# Simplify the function for the interval p <= x <= 15\nf_simplified = sp.simplify(f.subs({sp.Abs(x - p): x - p, sp.Abs(x - 15): 15 - x, sp.Abs(x - (p + 15)): (p + 15) - x}))\n\n# Find the minimum value of the simplified function in the interval p <= x <= 15\nmin_value = f_simplified.subs(x, 15)\n\nprint(min_value)\n```", "To determine the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - (p + 15)| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within the given interval.\n\nFirst, let's consider the critical points of the function. The function \\( f(x) \\) is composed of three absolute value terms, and the 